WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.711 --> 00:00:15.371
eyes lit up.

2
00:00:15.391 --> 00:00:18.513
"There's a victory tour after the Games?"

3
00:00:18.973 --> 00:00:19.433
he said.

4
00:00:19.453 --> 00:00:23.675
"Cool!" But Julia was horrified by the news.

5
00:00:23.695 --> 00:00:26.057
"What do you mean?"

6
00:00:26.677 --> 00:00:27.618
she asked Artemis.

7
00:00:29.278 --> 00:00:30.279
The goddess shrugged.

8
00:00:30.299 --> 00:00:31.800
"Just what I said.

9
00:00:32.352 --> 00:00:36.355
The Olympic champion always travels with his sponsor afterward."

10
00:00:36.375 --> 00:00:41.459
"The tour gets mortals quite excited," Hermes added with a grin.

11
00:00:43.121 --> 00:00:43.961
He looked at Brody.

12
00:00:43.981 --> 00:00:46.744
"You'll enjoy seeing more of the world, won't you, boy?"

13
00:00:46.764 --> 00:00:49.906
"Sure!" Brody said.

14
00:00:49.926 --> 00:00:52.528
"It sounds like the parade after the Super Bowl!"

15
00:00:54.029 --> 00:00:56.131
Julia was staring at Hermes in alarm.

16
00:00:56.151 --> 00:00:59.534
"But you said we could go home right after the Games."

17
00:00:59.554 --> 00:01:04.182
"Of course you can," Hermes told Julia soothingly.

18
00:01:04.202 --> 00:01:06.464
"Don't worry so much, mortal girl."

19
00:01:07.885 --> 00:01:10.407
Julia glanced away, trying to calm down.

20
00:01:11.869 --> 00:01:14.431
What if Hermes had been lying about letting them go home?

21
00:01:14.951 --> 00:01:16.793
What if they got stuck here forever?

22
00:01:16.813 --> 00:01:19.455
"This could be bad!"

23
00:01:19.956 --> 00:01:21.697
she whispered to Brody in a panic.

24
00:01:21.717 --> 00:01:24.860
"What are you talking about?"

25
00:01:25.321 --> 00:01:26.081
Brody asked.

26
00:01:27.402 --> 00:01:28.904
Julia kept her voice low.

27
00:01:29.372 --> 00:01:31.833
"What if Hermes is planning to keep us here?

28
00:01:32.393 --> 00:01:35.754
He and Caerus made it sound like the passage will eventually close.

29
00:01:36.034 --> 00:01:37.634
We could be stuck here forever!"

30
00:01:37.654 --> 00:01:40.815
"Whoa!" Brody said.

31
00:01:41.936 --> 00:01:47.037
For a second Julia thought she'd finally made him realize how serious this situation was.

32
00:01:48.117 --> 00:01:50.738
Then she saw that he was staring across the agora.

33
00:01:50.758 --> 00:01:53.399
"Who's that?"

34
00:01:53.959 --> 00:01:54.839
he blurted out.

35
00:01:55.999 --> 00:01:57.600
Another goddess was approaching them.

36
00:01:58.088 --> 00:02:01.029
She was blond and gorgeous, with big blue eyes.

37
00:02:01.049 --> 00:02:04.911
"Greetings, Aphrodite," Hermes called.

38
00:02:04.931 --> 00:02:06.531
"Come and meet my champion!"

39
00:02:07.672 --> 00:02:10.613
Aphrodite held out one pale, slim hand.

40
00:02:10.633 --> 00:02:12.494
"Hello, champion.

41
00:02:13.154 --> 00:02:13.894
It's a pleasure."

42
00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:18.276
"Uh, guh Brody said.

43
00:02:18.296 --> 00:02:19.817
"I mean, me too.

44
00:02:19.997 --> 00:02:21.057
I mean, hi!

45
00:02:21.397 --> 00:02:23.798
I'm Brody."

46
00:02:23.818 --> 00:02:27.400
"Brody," Aphrodite said with a musical laugh.

47
00:02:27.892 --> 00:02:29.232
"What a charming name."

48
00:02:30.673 --> 00:02:32.213
Julia moaned to herself.

49
00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:36.774
She could tell that Brody was already in love.

50
00:02:37.895 --> 00:02:40.676
Why were boys so easily distracted by a pretty face?

51
00:02:42.196 --> 00:02:44.717
"Have any of you seen Zeus' champion yet?"

52
00:02:45.237 --> 00:02:46.777
Aphrodite asked the other gods.

53
00:02:46.797 --> 00:02:49.118
"I hear he's very handsome.

54
00:02:49.638 --> 00:02:50.418
And strong."

55
00:02:50.438 --> 00:02:54.239
"Nobody has seen him," Artemis replied.

56
00:02:54.259 --> 00:02:56.540
"Zeus is hiding him in the hills."

57
00:02:58.208 --> 00:02:59.028
"That reminds me."

58
00:02:59.409 --> 00:03:01.330
Hermes grabbed Brody by the shoulder.

59
00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:03.010
"It's time for training.

60
00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:03.811
Let's go."

61
00:03:05.331 --> 00:03:06.972
"Are you sure we can't stay?"

62
00:03:07.432 --> 00:03:09.533
Brody was still staring at Aphrodite.

63
00:03:10.654 --> 00:03:15.376
Hermes pulled Brody away so fast that Julia and Markos had to run to keep up.

64
00:03:18.137 --> 00:03:20.778
Once again the gymnasium was filled with athletes.

65
00:03:21.979 --> 00:03:23.960
Hermes ordered Brody to start stretching.

66
00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:27.962
Brody dropped to the ground and touched his toes.

67
00:03:27.982 --> 00:03:30.804
"What are we working on today, Coach?"

68
00:03:31.285 --> 00:03:31.825
he asked.

69
00:03:31.845 --> 00:03:37.650
"We need to build your endurance for the dolichos and the hoplite," Hermes replied.

70
00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:43.895
"They are the longer and more difficult races, and I wasn't impressed with how quickly you became tired

71
00:03:43.935 --> 00:03:46.437
yesterday." "Quickly?"

72
00:03:46.997 --> 00:03:48.298
Brody sounded wounded.

73
00:03:48.318 --> 00:03:50.460
"You made me run for two hours straight!"

74
00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:55.184
"We should get out of the way," Markos said to Julia.

75
00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:57.621
"It's strange enough to have a girl here.

76
00:03:58.542 --> 00:04:01.864
We don't want anyone to think you're trying to compete or something."

77
00:04:04.785 --> 00:04:07.747
He laughed as if that was the funniest thing he'd ever imagined.

78
00:04:09.628 --> 00:04:12.630
Julia was getting tired of all the comments about girls.

79
00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:17.953
"It's not as if I'm the only girl here," she said, pointing.

80
00:04:19.114 --> 00:04:20.334
Markos shook his head.

81
00:04:20.354 --> 00:04:25.561
"That's not a girl—it's a goddess," he said.

82
00:04:25.581 --> 00:04:28.642
"It's Demeter training her champion."

83
00:04:28.662 --> 00:04:33.584
"Whatever." Julia followed Markos to some benches.

84
00:04:35.245 --> 00:04:37.266
They sat and watched Brody's workout.

85
00:04:38.406 --> 00:04:41.367
After a while Caerus arrived and waved to Hermes.

86
00:04:41.387 --> 00:04:45.129
"Take a quick rest, boy," Hermes told Brody.

87
00:04:45.149 --> 00:04:46.209
"I'll be back soon."

88
00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:49.050
He hurried off to talk to Caerus.

89
00:04:50.311 --> 00:04:54.085
Brody collapsed on the bench beside Julia, huffing and puffing.

90
00:04:55.226 --> 00:04:59.749
As soon as Markos hurried off to get Brody some water, Julia turned to Brody.

91
00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:03.532
"Listen, we need to talk," she said quickly.

92
00:05:03.552 --> 00:05:10.478
"If Hermes isn't going to let us go after the Games, there's no reason to stick around.

93
00:05:10.798 --> 00:05:13.300
We should try to escape as soon as possible."

94
00:05:15.382 --> 00:05:16.623
Brody didn't respond.

95
00:05:17.924 --> 00:05:19.425
He was peering toward the entrance.

96
00:05:19.445 --> 00:05:22.888
"Do you think Aphrodite has a champion?"

97
00:05:23.348 --> 00:05:23.888
he asked.

98
00:05:23.908 --> 00:05:25.809
"Maybe she'll bring him here to train.

99
00:05:26.129 --> 00:05:26.890
Do you think she will?"

100
00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:30.311
Just then Markos returned with the water.

101
00:05:30.751 --> 00:05:32.712
He saw Brody staring at Aphrodite.

102
00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:36.874
"Forget her," he warned Brody.

103
00:05:37.394 --> 00:05:38.214
"She's beautiful.

104
00:05:38.514 --> 00:05:39.575
But she's a goddess."

105
00:05:41.275 --> 00:05:42.756
Brody looked disappointed.

106
00:05:42.776 --> 00:05:47.378
"So I guess goddesses never, like, date mortals, huh?"

107
00:05:47.418 --> 00:05:48.258
Markos blinked.

108
00:05:48.278 --> 00:05:49.779
"Of course they do.

109
00:05:50.319 --> 00:05:52.360
But it never turns out very well for the mortal."

110
00:05:53.096 --> 00:05:55.237
He glanced around and lowered his voice.

111
00:05:55.257 --> 00:06:02.101
"According to the latest local gossip, Hera is very eager to see Zeus' new hero humiliated at the

112
00:06:02.141 --> 00:06:06.964
Games. Alcides is rumored to be Zeus' child born of a mortal woman.

113
00:06:07.344 --> 00:06:10.066
And we all know how jealous and vengeful Hera can be."

114
00:06:10.086 --> 00:06:11.907
"We do?"

115
00:06:12.327 --> 00:06:13.588
Brody looked confused.

116
00:06:13.608 --> 00:06:14.828
"Okay, whatever.

117
00:06:15.209 --> 00:06:20.952
Back to Aphrodite, I—" At that moment Hermes rushed over, looking excited.

118
00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:24.421
"Apollo just arrived with his champion," he said.

119
00:06:24.441 --> 00:06:26.823
"He's challenged us to a javelin contest.

120
00:06:27.383 --> 00:06:28.704
Come—it'll be good training."

121
00:06:30.124 --> 00:06:32.185
"Javelin? I've never done that before."

122
00:06:32.566 --> 00:06:33.306
Brody shrugged.

123
00:06:33.326 --> 00:06:35.947
"But it's just throwing a stick, right?

124
00:06:36.128 --> 00:06:36.908
How hard can it be?"

125
00:06:38.129 --> 00:06:39.169
He followed Hermes.

126
00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:42.011
Julia watched them go.

127
00:06:42.031 --> 00:06:46.533
"I can't believe Brody's being so stupid about all this!"

128
00:06:47.053 --> 00:06:48.254
she complained to Markos.

129
00:06:49.515 --> 00:06:51.496
Markos gave her an uneasy glance.

130
00:06:52.076 --> 00:06:54.538
"Perhaps we should watch the contest in silence."

131
00:06:55.818 --> 00:07:02.242
Halfway across the gymnasium, Brody and Hermes met up with Apollo and a tall teenager with broad shoulders

132
00:07:02.302 --> 00:07:03.002
and dark hair.

133
00:07:04.163 --> 00:07:05.884
The two boys picked up javelins.

134
00:07:07.025 --> 00:07:09.386
Apollo's champion handled his confidently.

135
00:07:10.447 --> 00:07:15.990
Brody fumbled with his javelin at first, but within moments he looked almost as comfortable as the other

136
00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:19.392
boy. Julia couldn't help being impressed.

137
00:07:20.348 --> 00:07:22.110
Brody really was a good athlete.

138
00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:28.015
"Too bad he doesn't have much brainpower to go with his athletic abilities," she thought.

139
00:07:28.035 --> 00:07:31.098
"Go!" Hermes called.

140
00:07:32.179 --> 00:07:34.120
Both athletes tossed their javelins.

141
00:07:35.321 --> 00:07:37.984
Julia blinked as the javelins flew through the air.

142
00:07:38.764 --> 00:07:46.431
Something about them looked strange… She gasped as both javelins transformed into enormous hissing snakes.

143
00:07:48.288 --> 00:07:52.478
They spun around in midair and flew straight back toward the boys!
